  <p class="eyebrow">Iterate hackathon, Track 4: World Models</p>
  <h1>How long can a generated world hold together while an agent plays in it?</h1>
  <p class="lede">We add inference-time memory, state tracking and re-anchoring to an open world model, with no training, to raise its <a href="https://kxding.github.io/project/PlayWorld/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PlayWorld</a> score above Genie 3 (2.12). Every number we report is scored by the benchmark's own Gemini 3.1 Pro verifier and traced to a commit. Reference rows come from the PlayWorld paper. Scores run from 1 to 5; higher is better.</p>
